            <div xml:id="d15">

                <pb facs="0080" n="15" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg15"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.0513/163: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Fish</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-09T17:00:00-04:00">July 9, 1936—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. Your 40, July 8, noon. The Department is disposed to refrain from pressing
                    the matter at this time provided the entire question can <pb facs="0081" n="16"
                        xml:id="pg16"/> be held in abeyance until Judge Booth’s return. However, if
                    the question is likely to be presented to the Council of Ministers for a
                    decision in the near future the Department would desire to submit this
                    Government’s views in order that they may be considered by the Council.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
